<h2 id='final-verdict'>🏁 Final Verdict</h2>

Moosend earns a genuine recommendation for aesthetics clinics in the small-to-mid-size range. Its automation builder is capable, its pricing is transparent and affordable, and the subscriber-based model rewards clinics that communicate frequently with their clients — which is exactly what effective retention marketing requires.

The integration gap with aesthetics booking platforms is a real limitation, not a minor footnote. If your practice's operational data lives in Jane App, Vagaro, or Mindbody, you will need a Zapier bridge or custom webhook setup to make Moosend's segmentation and triggers work properly. Build that setup cost into your evaluation.

For practices that are currently using Mailchimp on its most basic plan and not running any real automation, switching to Moosend's Pro plan is a meaningful upgrade in capability at a comparable or lower price point. For practices already running sophisticated multi-channel automation in Klaviyo or HubSpot, Moosend likely offers less than what you have.

At $9–$88/month depending on list size, and with a 30% lifetime discount available, the risk-to-reward ratio on a trial is close to zero. Run your post-treatment follow-up sequence in it for 30 days and you'll know quickly whether it handles your clinic's needs.

